//BUG="}} is taken as an escape inside a format expression, so a brace is lost"
//OUT="5}"

// `parse_format_string` (src/compiler/parser/out.rs) looks for `{{` and `}}`
// before it looks at whether it is inside a `{…}`. Here the first `}` should
// close the format and the `}}` after it should print one brace, as in Rust
// and Python. Instead the first two `}` are read as an escape, and the `}` it
// stands for is pushed onto the *expression* text, which becomes `x}`; the
// third `}` then closes the format. The stray `}` in `x}` is dropped by the
// defect in 43, so the program compiles and prints `5`, one brace short, with
// no error.
//
// `"{{{x}}}"` prints `{5` for the same reason. `{{` has no such problem in
// practice, because an expression never contains a `{`.
//
// The fix is to look for the escapes only while not inside a format.

fn main
    x = 5
    out "{x}}}"
